{"uid":"e309b40fe11ddf99","name":"test_the_shared_ralphctl_runner_keeps_the_tmp_home","fullName":"tests.test_engine_child_import_path#test_the_shared_ralphctl_runner_keeps_the_tmp_home","historyId":"005493f9df9f27af70fbabe93d2f1db3","time":{"start":1791921870198,"stop":1791921870533,"duration":335},"description":"`ralphctl` is the same package behind a second console script, and\n    the real `RALPHCTL` spawn -- exercised directly here rather than through\n    tests/test_cli_docker.py's `Ctl.run` (task 036 moved that shared helper\n    in-process, which would no longer touch this defect at all: this test's\n    whole subject IS the process boundary, so it keeps its own real spawn) --\n    lets a caller pass a HOME through. One import-path caller,\n    test_cli_resume_llm_wiring.py, asserts on the ~/.aws mount ralphctl\n    derives from that HOME, so it genuinely needs the override; before the\n    helper was applied there it failed with `ModuleNotFoundError: No module\n    named 'ralphd'` from ~/.local/bin/ralphctl line 3. Same defect, other\n    script.","descriptionHtml":"<p><code>ralphctl</code> is the same package behind a second console script, and<br />\nthe real <code>RALPHCTL</code> spawn -- exercised directly here rather than through<br />\ntests/test_cli_docker.py's <code>Ctl.run</code> (task 036 moved that shared helper<br />\nin-process, which would no longer touch this defect at all: this test's<br />\nwhole subject IS the process boundary, so it keeps its own real spawn) --<br />\nlets a caller pass a HOME through. One import-path caller,<br />\ntest_cli_resume_llm_wiring.py, asserts on the ~/.aws mount ralphctl<br />\nderives from that HOME, so it genuinely needs the override; before the<br />\nhelper was applied there it failed with <code>ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'ralphd'</code> from ~/.local/bin/ralphctl line 3. Same defect, other<br />\nscript.</p>\n","status":"passed","flaky":false,"newFailed":false,"newBroken":false,"newPassed":false,